From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:43:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: keep capture buffers across a drain

Capture buffers can be queued after the firmware has completed EOS but
before userspace has dequeued the LAST buffer. In the stopped state,
buf_queue returns every buffer to userspace empty, so these capture
buffers come back after V4L2_ENC_CMD_START as empty, non-LAST
completions with zero timestamps, which breaks matching encoded frames
to their source frames.

Only return output buffers in the stopped state. Capture buffers go on
the normal firmware queue and are used once encoding resumes.

Fixes: 7493db46e4c4 ("venus: venc: add handling for VIDIOC_ENCODER_CMD")
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index ca7009b8ec..984483a3bf 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -1336,7 +1336,9 @@ static void venc_vb2_buf_queue(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 
 	mutex_lock(&inst->lock);
 
-	if (inst->enc_state == VENUS_ENC_STATE_STOPPED) {
+	/* Capture buffers queued after EOS are needed when encoding resumes. */
+	if (inst->enc_state == VENUS_ENC_STATE_STOPPED &&
+	    V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(vb->type)) {
 		vbuf->sequence = inst->sequence_cap++;
 		vbuf->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
 		vb2_set_plane_payload(vb, 0, 0);
